    <macro_item guid="969aacc3-f2f2-4f4d-8176-44cc3b530e30" bitmap_id="83c742bf-9529-44d5-8bb8-7f76877d9e5d">
      <text>
        <locale_1033>MakeCrvPipe</locale_1033>
      </text>
      <tooltip>
        <locale_1033>Draw thin pipes along the curves on your [EDGE] layers so Enscape renders the edge.

Enscape will not show a line where two coplanar faces meet, which flattens joints and reveals
seams that should read as crisp. A slim pipe on the curve gives it something solid to shade.

Usage:
1. Put the curves you want to read as edges on a layer with [EDGE] in its name
2. Run the button; existing pipes are rebuilt rather than duplicated</locale_1033>
      </tooltip>
      <help_text>
        <locale_1033>Draw thin pipes along the curves on your [EDGE] layers so Enscape renders the edge.

